{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>11:4</b> The sense of \"He tests\": whether evil comes upon the righteous, it is to humble him and to try him and to prove him, in the manner of: \"for whom YHWH loves He proves\" (Proverbs 3:12). But the wicked He hates forever."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:59.503672959Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}